   "slot": "(b) the explanation",
   "desc": "Part (b): the student says what went wrong in the subtraction that produced 364. Full credit for naming the unpaid loan: a hundred was opened so that the empty tens column had something to give, but the hundreds digit was still worked as five instead of the four that were left, so the answer came out a whole hundred too big. Accept an answer that shows the correct regrouping -- four hundreds, nine tens, ten ones -- and points at the hundreds column as the one that disagrees. Half credit for saying only that the answer is too big by a hundred, without saying which column caused it. No credit for restating the correct difference, since part (a) already asks for it."
